00:00:04.390 --> 00:00:06.710 align:start position:0%
ukrainian army medics carry a wounded  soldier into a field hospital close to  the front line  a piece of shrapnel has ripped through  his side  the wound looks small but the sharp  metal fragment inside will kill him if  not dealt with fast  the medics pump the soldier with  anesthetic and pure oxygen  they pack the wound  he will be evacuated to a hospital  further back from the front line to have  the shrapnel removed  the teams say some nights they have to  treat up to 70 men wounded as they  defend their positions against the  russian army advance in a town close by  many of the medics have worked in  foreign war zones for decades but they  never expected one day they would be  saving lives at home  my whole professional life i've been  treating people i love people i love  life in all ways i chose my field  because death is the worst enemy  russians worst deed is that it turned me  a defender of life  into a killer  i have had to shoot in this war and most  likely i hit the target  some medics sleep in rooms next to the  makeshift trauma treatment area before  their shift starts  the shelves are full of medicine vital  for saving lives but  it's not medicine we need one of the  surgeons told me  it's weapons  more soldiers arrive  nurses prepare rehydration fluid others  search for veins in the men's arms so  they can fit cannulas and administer  medicine fast  the men are exhausted and dazed  we are tired and shell-shocked says this  soldier but it's to be expected of war  what's known  the most common injuries are from  shrapnel gunshot wounds blown off limbs  brain trauma and shell shock  we treat shell shock with simple  symptomatic medicines  there's not much else we can do  another soldier is brought in with a gun  shop wound under his arm the medics  calmly clean the area 55 year old lubima  seems relaxed but the bullet was only  millimeters away from potentially ending  his  life luberman took a gunshot wound  yesterday afternoon  the medics here say he is incredibly  lucky that that bullet did not sever the  archery in his arm  he will now go from here be taken from  here by ambulance  to one of the local hospitals further  back from the front line for further  treatment  some of the volunteers don't want to be  identified because they say russian  forces are targeting medics treating  ukrainian soldiers  after being treated lubimir eats  breakfast while waiting to be evacuated  before the war he was a construction  worker renovating the chernobyl nuclear  plant  their mortar guys can get really close  to us and they're difficult to see and  shoot they approach our trenches and  throw grenades before lunch yesterday  there were 50 shells that hit near our  position  russian artillery shells and mortars  target ukrainian positions in fields  close by  no one knows how many wounded will be  brought to the field hospital  in the hours ahead  charles stratford al jazeera eastern  ukraine
 

